DriftWM
-------
Upstream: https://github.com/malbiruk/driftwm
Maintainer: Maksim Kononenko (malbiruk), with contributors. GPL-3.0-or-later.
Pins: each derived file names the commit it was adapted at, either
df3de27b26c7998e8a460cffd8a4925cbed3a322 (DriftWM v0.21.0, the baseline of
crates/core) or 352333a8fa1b22171492d4b71a54102045c9a19d (the commit the first
port started from). The files that name only 352333a8 are crates/canvas/src, the
crates/desktop/src modules and the native/desktop files listed below that were
written at that port; crates/core/PORT.md records the hashes and deviations of
crates/core.
The GPL version 3 text in LICENSE is copied unchanged from the baseline.

This is a new Rust/Objective-C implementation informed by DriftWM's infinite
canvas design. It does not compile or run the upstream Wayland/Smithay
compositor on macOS. Files derived from DriftWM (each names the upstream
repository, commit and path in its header or, in native/desktop, at the adapted
block or section):
  crates/core/                  the pure modules: canvas, config, layout, the
                                direction_from_vector gesture helper, platform
                                stand-ins and keysym lookup, with their tests;
                                crates/core/PORT.md lists every hash and deviation
  crates/canvas/src/            cluster_resize, geometry, gestures, layout, lib, stage
  crates/desktop/src/           actions, bindings, effects, fullscreen, gestures,
                                ipc, ipc_client, keyboard_layout, keyboard_snap,
                                lifecycle, motion, navigation, output_actions,
                                passthrough, pointer_policy, render,
                                resize_transaction, rules, settings, sizes,
                                storage, taps, view_actions, window_actions
  native/desktop/               background, background-tiff, compositor,
                                canvas-renderer, cycle-hold, frame-driver,
                                hot-corners, hotkeys, input-sources, ipc-server,
                                main, pan-launch, pointer-hover,
                                screenshot-writer, tap-keys, trackpad-gestures,
                                window-manager
  crates/core/config.reference.toml and the two proptest seed files
  crates/core/proptest-regressions/layout/fill.txt and snap.txt are byte copies
  of the baseline files and crates/core/docs/window-rules.md is the baseline page with six relative links
  made absolute (see crates/core/PORT.md); the oracle copies under
  crates/canvas/tests/upstream, crates/desktop/tests/upstream and
  crates/desktop/tests/resize_upstream are upstream excerpts, each directory
  with a SHA256SUMS.

Sunlight
--------
Upstream: https://github.com/spacefarm-digital/sunlight
Commit: afeea74b18e70ca49bf462d6fe462cf65deb2b32
Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 spacefarm. The licence text is
native/desktop/SUNLIGHT-NOTICE.txt, which the app bundle carries beside this
file. Each adapted file names what it took. Files derived from Sunlight:
  native/desktop/multitouch-source.m, dock-guard.m, dock-control.h and
  trackpad-gestures.m adapt Sources/Canvas/TrackpadPan.swift: reading trackpad
  contacts through MultitouchSupport, a session event tap that holds back
  Dock-control events, and the spread rule.
  native/desktop/system-takeover.m translates, function by function,
  Sources/Canvas/Takeover/SystemPrefs.swift and TakeoverMode.swift: snapshot the
  user's own preferences before the first write, an absent key restored as
  absent, restore on every end and from a leftover record at the next launch.
  native/desktop/window-events.m and window-events.h adapt
  Sources/Canvas/RealWindows/WindowServerEvents.swift (SkyLight's window-created
  event and its payload).
  The arrival veil of native/privileged/payload.m adapts the same event
  source and the aim of LiveWindows/osax/sunbeam.h that a new window is never
  seen before it is placed (native/privileged/protocol.h carries its constants).
  Compositor mode at login: native/privileged/loadd.m copies LiveWindows/helper.m
  (the daemon, its XPC listener and caller requirement, with the edits its header
  lists); native/privileged/loadd-request.m borrows the caller-requirement form;
  native/desktop/loader-service.m and native/desktop/dock-reload.m (with
  dock-reload.h and dock-reload-regression.m) translate
  Sources/Canvas/Setup/LiveWindowsService.swift,
  Sources/Canvas/RealWindows/AdditionReloader.swift (including DockCrashGuard) and
  Tests/CanvasTests/AdditionReloaderTests.swift; native/privileged/com.marengox.infinify.loader.plist
  adapts Resources/LaunchDaemons/com.spacefarm.sunlight.live-windows.plist.
  native/privileged/loader.m also cites Sunlight.

yabai
-----
Upstream: https://github.com/asmvik/yabai (https://github.com/koekeishiya/yabai
redirects to it). Commit: dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd.
Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Åsmund Vikane. The licence text, with the
provenance of the window-server query and the window-forward calls, is
native/desktop/YABAI-NOTICE.txt, which the app bundle carries beside this file.
Each adapted file names the upstream paths it follows. Files derived from yabai:
  native/privileged/loader.m is adapted from yabai and retains its MIT licence,
  copyright and Jeremy Legendre arm64e attribution; payload.m
  cites the same commit for the Dock-side calls. native/privileged/loadd.m reaches
  yabai's src/sa.m by way of Sunlight's LiveWindows/helper.m (see Sunlight above)
  and pins only the Sunlight commit.
  native/desktop/window-events.m, window-events.h and the event handling of
  native/desktop/window-manager.m (src/workspace.m, src/application.c,
  src/application.h, src/window.c, src/window.h, src/event_loop.c,
  src/window_manager.c: which notifications an application and a window are
  observed with, and what each one means).
  native/desktop/window-server-family.h (src/window.c:872-897,
  src/misc/extern.h:9,66-72, src/window_manager.c:841-855), used by
  native-family.m, native-display-space.m, native-placement-validation.m and
  native-presenter.m.
  native/focus/focus.m brings a window that is on another desktop forward with the
  calls and the event record of window_manager_focus_window_with_raise and
  window_manager_make_key_window (src/window_manager.c:1269-1335,
  src/misc/extern.h:81-82, src/window_manager.h:5).
  native/resize/resize.m cites the same commit.

